SUMMARY:Inprint Ayad Akhtar Reading
DTSTAMP:20260724T105422Z
DTSTART:20261005T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:General admission tickets will go on sale on Tuesday\, Septembe
	r 15\, 2026 at 12 pm. \nAyad Akhtar will read from his new novel The Radia
	nce\, followed by an on-stage conversation led by a local author/journalis
	t. The evening will conclude with a book sale and signing. The event is pr
	esented as part of the 2026/2027 Inprint Margarett Root Brown Reading Seri
	es.  \nPulitzer Prize winner Ayad Akhtar’s new novel The Radiance is “simp
	ly put\, a work of genius… Akhtar explores the nature of memory and of the
	 soul\, while the unfolding tale builds tension and anticipation like a wh
	odunit” (Abraham Verghese). It has been named one of the New York Time‘s “
	Novels Everyone Will Be Talking About in 2026.” A mysterious accident alon
	g a country road sparks an awakening and an investigation in Akhtar’s most
	 daring work yet—a visionary novel of spiritual transformation in an age o
	f fracture. \nAkhtar’s work as a novelist and playwright has been publishe
	d and performed in over two dozen languages. He is the winner of the Pulit
	zer Prize for Drama for his play Disgraced\, which was also nominated for 
	the Tony Award for Best Play. His other Broadway plays include McNeal\, Ju
	nk\, and The Who & The What. Akhtar is also the author of the novels Ameri
	can Dervish\, a Kirkus Reviews Best Book of the Year\, and Homeland Elegie
	s\, called “a tour de force” by The Washington Post. In 2021\, he was name
	d the New York State Author by the New York State Writers Institute\, succ
	eeding Colson Whitehead. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-ay
	ad-akhtar-reading/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/inprint-ayad-akhtar-reading/
LOCATION:Alley Theatre\, 615 Texas Avenue\, Houston\, TX\, 77002
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
